## 2. What each block exposes (12 October 2026)

Every block follows the A0 contract. `block.py` is the only source: its `META`, its `PARAMS` (name, unit, min, max, default, lin or log scale, description), an optional `FIT` dict of fitter hints, and a torch `render`. `block.json` and `demo.wav` are generated from it by `BuildSoundBank.py`. Every block has 7 or 8 parameters, no more than the HDA limit of 8 per category. All 27 are original code derived from the mathematics, so `licence` is `original` and no third-party code was copied. (12 October 2026)

The patterned blocks are deterministic patterns, not random ones, as the task asked. `keyboard_typing` has count, rate, jitter and accent parameters over an R1 low-discrepancy sequence. `glitch_stutter` has rate, count, density and pitch spread. `shaker` has count, rate and swing. `static_crackle` has density and click duration. Each stroke is a template with its own fixed noise, placed by an exact fractional delay in the frequency domain (`sfxdsp.delay_sum`). The count is continuous, with the last stroke faded in by its fraction, so every parameter keeps a gradient. (12 October 2026)

## 3. What had to change in the fitter, and why (12 October 2026)

The first full run (`verify-run1.json`, 3378 s) failed on 20 of 81 recover cases. The pattern blocks were worst: glitch_stutter at 0.02, keyboard_typing at 10.3 and shaker at 0.14. Three causes were measured and fixed, all as additions that the A0 blocks do not trigger. (12 October 2026)

- **Stroke patterns have no gradient from far away.** A click train shifted by more than one stroke width gets no gradient back towards its place. `ploss.time_blur_error` adds an envelope term on a power envelope smoothed by a Gaussian in time. A block opts in through `FIT` (`screenBlurMs`, `blurStartMs`, `blurEndMs`), and the blur is annealed to 2 ms the same way A0 anneals its frequency blur. It never counts in the score. (12 October 2026)
- **One parameter stuck in a wrong basin.** Most misses after that were a single parameter in a wrong basin, or two parameters that trade against each other: onset against attack, tail level against overall level, hi-hat base pitch against metal level. `dfit` gained a coordinate scan, level-matched scans that refit the level while scanning another parameter, and pair scans declared per block (`scanPairs`). (12 October 2026)
- **Joint refinement.** A joint evolution strategy over the parameter groups, then a box CMA-ES on the official E2 from the best state, one run per sigma of `dfit.cmaSigmas`. Both use a fixed seed. CMA-ES is written from the published algorithm (Hansen), not copied. (12 October 2026)

The shaker was the last to resist (`verify-shaker.json`: 98.78 and 78.47). Its grains now peak a fixed time after their stroke, whatever their attack, so attack no longer moves the onset. With a larger budget declared in its `FIT`, it reaches 99.69. It is also by far the slowest block to fit, at 6524 s for three cases. (12 October 2026)

`VerifySoundBank.py` gained a `--cross contrast` mode. Each red target is checked against an explicit list of wrong blocks, because the all-against-all cross fits of A0 grow as N squared once the bank holds about 50 blocks. `FitBankCases.py` reruns selected recover cases in parallel. All new settings live in `datasets/sfx-params.json`. (12 October 2026)

