## 5. Limits, measured (13 October 2026)

- **The two scores disagree on four blocks.** The ploss score and the B1 descriptor score agree on 23 of the 27 blocks. On four they do not, even though the ploss fit is at least 99.95: key_press scores 0.00 in B1, ui_tick 51.94, impact_layered 65.13 and wind 79.99. Each of these is two events (press and release, two pings), a layered sound, or a stationary noise. B1's descriptors were tuned on single events, so they score these sounds poorly. A ploss score of 99.95 means the spectrogram and the envelope match; it does not mean B1's descriptors do. This is reported, not hidden. (13 October 2026)
- **Self-recovery is not reproduction.** As in A0, every target here was rendered by the bank with the same noise seed. On real sounds, the A3 calibration run (`/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-motion-design/docs/build/A3-calibration.md`) fitted 180 CC0 Kenney sounds with the 47 A1 and A2 source blocks. It reached a median of 82.29 on the seed-invariant metric and 47.22 on the official one, and no sound reached 99. The bank is still far from a 1:1 reproduction of real SFX, and the next work is chains, layering and the stochastic metric, not more self-tests. (13 October 2026)
- **Fit cost.** Pattern blocks take minutes to tens of minutes per fit on one CPU thread (shaker about 36 min per case). Any later loop on real targets needs these budgets kept per block in `FIT`. (12 October 2026)

